cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "The Energy Balance Project (EBU): a homeostatic field model and local actor-motion law"
abstract: >-
  A small, self-contained research model of homeostasis on a graph: can purely local
  rules keep a resource field viable indefinitely, with no central optimizer? Includes a
  conservation-audited simulation engine, a safe discrete movement law, regeneration
  (logistic/Allee/finite sources), protective harvest rules, and an EBU accounting layer
  whose guarded ledger (live-state causal credit against a threshold-aware burden, with
  transport and irreversible-extraction debits) closes gaming attacks that a naive ledger
  admits, without altering the underlying physics. Version 2.7 adds a mathematical
  foundation note (no engine change): the local actor law is derived as gradient flow
  of a state functional under a dissipation potential, with a continuous-time
  energy-dissipation (Lyapunov) theorem and numerical regression validation. Version
  2.8 adds a synchronous discrete mathematical foundation (draft, not peer reviewed;
  no engine change) for the idealised Model D0 discretisation only - a one-step
  energy-dissipation inequality with explicit finite-step remainder, corrected
  curvature constant, and spectral step-size bounds - together with standard-library
  numerical validation (132 checks); the production engine family is explicitly out
  of scope and numerical validation is not proof. Version 2.9 implements the exact
  synchronous local D0 law as a strict-locality engine and adds P1C, a source-local
  preservation controller: a robust aggregate safe-export budget, proportional
  multi-edge allocation, post-loss service accounting, and explicit unmet demand,
  carrying a one-step reserve-preservation theorem (outside the V2.8 theorem; the
  joint constrained descent theorem remains open). Preregistered deterministic
  studies (D1-D8 wind tunnel, D9 Allee reserve stress, D10 140-run phase map) show,
  in these fixtures only, that the hard local cap preserves the source at its
  certified reserve with zero crossings and zero physical over-use while rationing
  infeasible demand honestly, where soft penalties and unconstrained flow collapse.
  Deterministic validation only, not peer reviewed; no EBU issuance, debt ledger,
  wallet, or scalarisation is implemented, and numerical validation is not proof.
authors:
